<title>USA: MBL Life Assurance cuts real estate assets $1bln.</title>
<headline>MBL Life Assurance cuts real estate assets $1bln.</headline>
<dateline>NEWARK, N.J. 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>MBL Life Assurance Corp said on Thursday its total adjusted capital increased by $111 million, to $394 million, in 1996, while the company reduced its portfolio of real-estate-related assets by more than $1 billion.</p>
<p>MBL Life assumed and reinsured the insurance liabilities and most of the assets of Mutual Benefit Life Insurance Co in 1994 under a court-approved rehabilitation plan that is in effect through 1999.</p>
<p>The company said its real-estate portfolio has been reduced to $700 million from a high of more than $5 billion in 1991.</p>
<p>Thursday, 6 March 1997 16:50:09</p>
